    <h1>Tiananmen Square Massacre Timeline (April-June 1989)</h1>

    <div class="timeline">
        <div class="event">
            <div class="date">April 15, 1989</div>
            <p>Death of former Communist Party General Secretary Hu Yaobang, who was seen as a reformer. Students begin gathering in Tiananmen Square to mourn him and call for reforms.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="event">
            <div class="date">April 18-21, 1989</div>
            <p>Student demonstrations grow in size. Students demand official recognition of their movement, freedom of the press, and an end to corruption.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="event">
            <div class="date">April 22, 1989</div>
            <p>Hu Yaobang's funeral is held without student participation. Students stage a silent protest outside the Great Hall of the People.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="event">
            <div class="date">April 26, 1989</div>
            <p>People's Daily publishes an editorial calling the protests "turmoil" fomented by "a small minority of people with ulterior motives." This sparks larger demonstrations.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="event">
            <div class="date">May 4, 1989</div>
            <p>Over 100,000 students and supporters march through Beijing, marking the 70th anniversary of the May Fourth Movement.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="event">
            <div class="date">May 13, 1989</div>
            <p>Students begin a hunger strike in Tiananmen Square to pressure the government. The strike draws international attention.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="event">
            <div class="date">May 19, 1989</div>
            <p>General Secretary Zhao Ziyang makes an emotional appeal to the students to end their hunger strike. He is later purged for his sympathetic stance.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="event">
            <div class="date">May 20, 1989</div>
            <p>Martial law is declared in Beijing. Troops begin moving toward the city but are blocked by citizens.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="event">
            <div class="date">June 3-4, 1989</div>
