        </div>

        <div class="event">
            <div class="date">June 9, 1989</div>
            <p>Deng Xiaoping declares the protests a "counter-revolutionary rebellion" and praises the military's actions.</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="note">
        <p><strong>Note:</strong> The exact death toll remains disputed. Chinese government sources report around 200 deaths, while other estimates range up to 3,000 or more. The events are officially referred to in China as the "June Fourth Incident" and are heavily censored in Chinese media.</p>
    </div>
